From 006879cb2709c0fa977467799dca485c150b2785 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: grep <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 20:16:42 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] vayu-0151: Novatek NT36672C touch over QUPv3 SE17 SPI

Port of the vayu Linux nt36672c driver's protocol: SE17 clocks (gcc
wrap2 s0 + AHB votes, RCG at XO), pins 55-58 qup17, reset GPIO12, GENI
SPI in polled FIFO mode (mode 0, 4.8 MHz), chip id (NT36672A family
map), host download of the flashless IC's firmware with hardware CRC
(firmware from the ADT /vayu-touch fw01/fw02, panel from vayupanel=),
then 6-byte point records polled every 8 ms into sweet_hid_touch().
---
 bsd/conf/files        |   1 +
 bsd/dev/sweet_touch.c |   9 +-
 bsd/dev/vayu_touch.c  | 748 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 3 files changed, 754 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)
 create mode 100644 bsd/dev/vayu_touch.c

